{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-09-02T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"September's National Mushroom Month celebrates a world that often goes unnoticed. Beneath forest floors, lawns, and fallen leaves, fungal networks recycle nutrients, helping ecosystems thrive. The mushrooms we notice are only the fruiting bodies of these hidden organisms, emerging briefly to release spores before fading back from view. They are not plants; fungi form a kingdom of their own and play an essential role in nature's cycles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-US3885857486_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HorseHairShroom_EN-US3885857486_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A world beneath your feet","Title":"Horsehair parachute fungus, Belarus","Copyright":"© Máté/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In southeastern Pennsylvania, Kennett Square has earned a global reputation as the 'Mushroom Capital of the World.'","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=National+Mushroom+Month&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260901_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260901_HorseHairShroom"},"Ssd":"20260901","Name":"HorseHairShroom","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3885857486","FullDateString":"Sep 1, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Stand in Registan Square and it's easy to see why it is considered the architectural heart of Samarkand—one of Central Asia's oldest cities. This plaza in Uzbekistan is framed by three magnificent madrasas—Islamic centers of learning—whose soaring portals draw the eye upward. Yet some of the square's greatest treasures reveal themselves only when you look closer.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-US3761829748_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SamarkandCeiling_EN-US3761829748_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A master class in pattern","Title":"Building detail of Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan","Copyright":"© Piero M. Bianchi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/39.655009,66.975755/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=39.655009,66.975755;S9;Registan Square, Samarkand, Uzbekistan&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Samarkand&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260831_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260831_SamarkandCeiling"},"Ssd":"20260831","Name":"SamarkandCeiling","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3761829748","FullDateString":"Aug 31, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today, International Whale Shark Day makes room for the world's largest fish. Despite their name, whale sharks are not whales but fish, reaching lengths of up to 60 feet and weighing around 20 tons. Found in warm tropical seas, they glide through the water with their mouths open, filtering plankton, fish eggs, and other tiny prey. This species' distinctive white-spot patterns are unique to each individual, much like human fingerprints.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-US3678567058_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowShark_EN-US3678567058_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The fish that outgrew its name","Title":"Whale shark and golden trevally, Cenderawasih Bay, West Papua, Indonesia","Copyright":"© Pete Oxford/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Whale sharks may live for a century or more, giving the world's largest fish an unexpectedly long life span.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=whale+shark&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260830_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260830_YellowShark"},"Ssd":"20260830","Name":"YellowShark","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3678567058","FullDateString":"Aug 30, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off the coast of Santa Catarina, a state in southern Brazil, the image captures a familiar ritual: surfers waiting beyond the breaking waves, their boards rising and falling with the Atlantic. From above, almost nothing seems to happen. But that's when the real work begins.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-US3600536393_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatarina_EN-US3600536393_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Reading between the waves","Title":"Aerial view of surfers, Santa Catarina, Brazil","Copyright":"© Wonderful Nature/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-27.374188,-48.654926/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-27.374188,-48.654926;S9;Santa Catarina, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brazil+Santa+Catarina&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260829_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260829_SantaCatarina"},"Ssd":"20260829","Name":"SantaCatarina","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3600536393","FullDateString":"Aug 29, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunset, Mont-Saint Michel rises from the waters of Normandy, France, like a fortress shaped by the sea. Perched on a rocky tidal island, the abbey and village stand at the center of one of Europe's most dramatic coastal settings. Twice a day, the sea retreats to reveal vast stretches of sand before surging back to reclaim the landscape. At high tide, the mount becomes an island once again. For centuries, travelers timed their journeys to this rhythm, crossing the flats when conditions allowed and watching the sea return hours later.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-US3527235033_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MichelSunset_EN-US3527235033_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where tides shape a legend","Title":"Mont-Saint-Michel during high tide, Manche, Normandy, France","Copyright":"© Clement LEONARD/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.637417,-1.5112/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.637417,-1.5112;S9;Mont-Saint-Michel, Normandy, France&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mont+Saint+Michel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260828_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260828_MichelSunset"},"Ssd":"20260828","Name":"MichelSunset","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3527235033","FullDateString":"Aug 28, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a world without the natural wonders that hold about 90% of Earth's surface freshwater. Lakes are among our planet's most valuable resources. They provide clean water, support wildlife, help regulate climate, and sustain communities around the globe. In recognition of their vital role, the United Nations designated August 27 as World Lake Day, first observed in 2025. The need for action is greater than ever. More than 117 million lakes cover nearly 4% of Earth's land surface, yet many face growing pressure from pollution, overuse, and climate change.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-US3401664434_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeMagadi_EN-US3401664434_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Water, wildlife, and wonder","Title":"Lesser flamingo flock at sunrise, Lake Magadi, Kenya","Copyright":"© Denis-Huot/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-1.902409,36.265224/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-1.902409,36.265224;S9;Lake Magadi, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Lake+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260827_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260827_LakeMagadi"},"Ssd":"20260827","Name":"LakeMagadi","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3401664434","FullDateString":"Aug 27, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As darker nights return to Iceland, visitors will soon look to the skies for a chance to see the aurora borealis. Better known as the northern lights, this luminous phenomenon occurs when particles from the sun interact with gases high in Earth's atmosphere, creating shimmering ribbons of green, pink, purple, and sometimes red light. Iceland's northern location and increasingly dark autumn and winter nights make it one of the world's premier destinations for aurora viewing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-US3293282785_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AurorasIceland_EN-US3293282785_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A sky alive with color","Title":"Auroras over Kirkjufell, Iceland","Copyright":"© Cavan Images/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/64.939949,-23.307478/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=64.939949,-23.307478;S9;Kirkjufell, Iceland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Aurora+borealis&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260826_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260826_AurorasIceland"},"Ssd":"20260826","Name":"AurorasIceland","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3293282785","FullDateString":"Aug 26, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A beech tree stands alone amid golden fields near East Meon in Hampshire, providing a striking focal point in the rolling landscape of England's South Downs National Park. Agriculture has shaped these chalk hills for centuries, and farming remains an important part of the region today. The area's free-draining chalk soils support extensive arable farming, with wheat and barley among the most common crops. Throughout the summer, these crops ripen in the fields before harvest transforms the countryside into a patchwork of gold and stubble.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_EN-US4535769514_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BeechEngland_EN-US4535769514_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Fields of gold","Title":"Beech tree in a cereal field, East Meon, South Downs National Park, Hampshire, England","Copyright":"© Guy Edwardes/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.994476,-1.03351/8?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.994476,-1.03351;S9;East Meon, Hampshire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hampshire+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260908_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260908_BeechEngland"},"Ssd":"20260908","Name":"BeechEngland","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"4535769514","FullDateString":"Sep 8, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Labor Day honors the contributions of American workers and the history of labor in the United States. Established as a federal holiday in 1894, it emerged during a period of rapid industrial growth and social change. Today, Labor Day recognizes the people whose efforts have helped build communities, industries, and infrastructure across the nation. From farms and factories to railroads and construction sites, generations of workers have played a vital role in shaping the country's history.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RalphStackpole_EN-US4463800234_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RalphStackpole_EN-US4463800234_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Labor's legacy","Title":"'Industries of California' mural by Ralph Stackpole at Coit Tower, San Francisco, California","Copyright":"© David R. Frazier Photolibrary, Inc./Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.802705,-122.405821/7?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.802705,-122.405821;S9;Coit Tower, San Francisco, California&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260907_RalphStackpole\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Labor+Day+US&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260907_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260907_RalphStackpole"},"Ssd":"20260907","Name":"RalphStackpole","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"4463800234","FullDateString":"Sep 7, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, today's image looks more like a drowned woodland than a lake. Bare tree trunks emerge from the water, their reflections stretching across the surface as the Grampians glow in the distance. This is Lake Fyans, an artificial reservoir on the edge of the Grampians (Gariwerd) National Park in Victoria, Australia. Popular with boaters, anglers, sailors, and water-skiers, it offers a front-row seat to one of the country's most striking landscapes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_EN-US4295341714_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LakeFyans_EN-US4295341714_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A reservoir of reflections","Title":"Lake Fyans, Grampians National Park, Victoria, Australia","Copyright":"© tracielouise/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-37.1431,142.6352/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-37.1431,142.6352;S9;Lake Fyans, Grampians National Park, Victoria, Australia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grampians+National+Park+Victoria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260906_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260906_LakeFyans"},"Ssd":"20260906","Name":"LakeFyans","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"4295341714","FullDateString":"Sep 6, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"National Hummingbird Day celebrates some of nature's most extraordinary aerial specialists. Found only in the Americas, these tiny birds can hover in place, fly backward, and beat their wings dozens of times per second. As they visit flowers in search of nectar, they also serve as important pollinators, helping sustain ecosystems from alpine meadows to tropical rainforests. Their shimmering plumage, remarkable agility, and high-energy lifestyles make them some of the world's most fascinating birds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_EN-US3119017947_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GreenCrowned_EN-US3119017947_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Small birds, big impact","Title":"Green-crowned brilliant hummingbirds feeding on lobster-claw flowers, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Paul Hobson/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"With the highest metabolic rate of any vertebrate, hummingbirds may need to feed every 10 minutes.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=National+Hummingbird+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260905_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260905_GreenCrowned"},"Ssd":"20260905","Name":"GreenCrowned","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3119017947","FullDateString":"Sep 5, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Rising above the salt marshes along Germany's North Sea coast, the Westerheversand Lighthouse is instantly recognizable thanks to its distinctive red-and-white stripes. Built between 1906 and 1908, the lighthouse has stood as an icon on the Eiderstedt Peninsula for more than a century, guiding ships through the waters of the North Sea. Today, it remains one of northern Germany's best-known coastal landmarks. Visitors who climb its 157 steps are rewarded with sweeping views of the surrounding scenery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-US3028839945_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Westerheversand_EN-US3028839945_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Red and white on the horizon","Title":"Westerheversand Lighthouse in Westerhever, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany","Copyright":"© bluejayphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.373402,8.6399/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.373402,8.6399;S9;Westerheversand Lighthouse, Schleswig-Holstein, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Westerheversand+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260904_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260904_Westerheversand"},"Ssd":"20260904","Name":"Westerheversand","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"3028839945","FullDateString":"Sep 4, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Waves usually belong to the ocean. In northern Arizona, they rise from the desert instead. The swirling sandstone formations of Coyote Buttes, part of Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, were shaped by ancient dunes and millions of years of erosion, creating a landscape that seems to ripple even while standing still.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_EN-US4070936347_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AZWilderness_EN-US4070936347_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"An act of wilderness","Title":"Coyote Buttes, Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona","Copyright":"© James Hager/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.7783,-111.7361/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-US&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.7783,-111.7361;S9;Vermilion Cliffs National Monument, Arizona&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wilderness+Act+of+1964&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260903_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260903_AZWilderness"},"Ssd":"20260903","Name":"AZWilderness","Market":"EN-US","Hash":"4070936347","FullDateString":"Sep 3, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Along England's east shore, the Suffolk Heritage Coast blends windswept heaths, marshes, shingle beaches, and expansive North Sea views. One of its best-known towns is Southwold, where water and history are inseparable. Almost encircled by the sea, the River Blyth, and surrounding wetlands, the town occupies a slender peninsula shaped by centuries of fishing, trade, and life at the edge of the water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-US3987062531_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SuffolkHuts_EN-US3987062531_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Painted along the shore","Title":"Traditional beach huts, Southwold, Suffolk Heritage Coast, England","Copyright":"© stevendocwra/Getty I